Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Office document file-type associations for the em Client CrossOver/Wine bottle.
;
; Not something the eM Client installer sets up itself (unlike .pdf, which ships
; associated with pdffile -> winebrowser.exe out of the box on a fresh CrossOver
; bottle) -- confirmed missing for .docx specifically (see
; reports/office-file-associations-findings.md), which is why em Client's own
; Explorer-mirroring open logic (MailClient.UI.ShellInterop.OpenItem, with a
; Process.Start/"openas" fallback) has nothing to resolve and Wine's shell32 shows
; its own "There is no Windows program configured to open this type of file."
; message box.
;
; Each extension gets its own ProgID under the EMClientWinePort.<ext> namespace --
; deliberately not reusing any real Microsoft Office/LibreOffice ProgID name, so
; these entries can never collide with (or be mistaken for) a genuine Office suite
; installed in the same bottle later. All of them point at the same handler already
; proven to work for .pdf: winebrowser.exe, which hands the file to the host's
; xdg-open/MIME-configured Linux viewer.
;
; releases/<version>/deploy.sh imports this file selectively at deploy time (only
; the extensions not already associated with something, unless --force-associations
; is passed) rather than a blind `wine regedit /S` of the whole thing -- see its
; own comments for how the selective merge works. This full file is also valid to
; import as-is by hand (`wine regedit /S file-associations/office-associations.reg`)
; if you want every entry unconditionally, overwriting anything already there.

; --- Microsoft Word ---
[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\.doc]
@="EMClientWinePort.doc"

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\EMClientWinePort.doc\shell\open\command]
@="\"c:\\windows\\system32\\winebrowser.exe\" \"%1\""

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\.docx]
@="EMClientWinePort.docx"

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\EMClientWinePort.docx\shell\open\command]
@="\"c:\\windows\\system32\\winebrowser.exe\" \"%1\""

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\.docm]
@="EMClientWinePort.docm"

[HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\EMClientWinePort.docm\shell\open\command]
@="\"c:\\windows\\system32\\winebrowser.exe\" \"%1\""

